ning hands. Since I have no melds, it's all about the tiles I have. Let's see:\n\n- All Chows (4 points): four chows and a pair. But I don't see enough suited tiles for that. For example, in Characters, I have 1, 2, 6, 8. Not enough for chows. Dots have 3,4,7. Maybe 3-4-5? No 5. 7-8-9? No 8 or 9. So probably not All Chows.\n\n- Mixed Straight (8 points): chows of 1-2-3, 4-5-6, 7-8-9 in different suits. Let's see. Do I have enough? For example, in Characters, 1,2 could be part of 1-2-3 if I had a 3. But I don't. Dots have 3,4,7. Maybe not. Not likely.\n\n- Mixed Triple Chow (8 points): three chows in different suits with same numbers. Not seeing that here.\n\n- Mixed Shifted Pungs (8 points): three pungs in different suits with consecutive numbers. Not applicable here since I have no pungs.\n\n- Half Flush (6 points): all honor and one suit. I have honors and multiple suits, so no.\n\n- All Types (6 points): all three suits and honors. Yes, I have W, T, B, F, J. So that's 6 points.\n\n- Outside Hand (4 points): all melds and pair have terminals or honors. Let's see. If my pair is T6 or B7 (which are non-terminals), then not. But if I can form a pair with a terminal, but I don't have any 1 or 9 in suited tiles except W1 (1), but it's only one. So maybe not. So Outside Hand might not apply.\n\n- Fully Concealed Hand (4 points): yes, since all melds are concealed. So that's 4 points.\n\n- All Chows (2 points): as discussed, probably not.\n\n- All Simples (2 points): no, because I have W1 (terminal) and W8 (not terminal, but 8 is not 9). Wait, terminals are 1 and 9. So W1 is a terminal. The rest are simples. So if I have a pair of non-terminals, then All Simples would be 2 points. But I need to check if all tiles are simples except the pair. Let's see: the pair could be T6 (simple), B7 (simple). Then the rest are W1 (terminal), W2, W6, W8 (simples), T6 (simple), B3, B4, B7 (simples). So yes, All Simples would apply here. So that's 2 points.\n\nSo total points from these: