ct supports the chows, while retaining T6/B7 for possible pairs. Discarding J2 also avoids giving others a chance to complete a Little Three Dragons pattern if they need it.\n\nReason: Discarding J2 removes an honor tile that doesn\u2019t contribute to chows or pungs, preserves the B1-B4 sequence for potential chows, and avoids aiding opponents in scoring patterns like Little Three Dragons. The remaining tiles (W1, W2, W6, W8, T6, T6, B1-B4, B7-B7, F3) can still form a viable hand with two chows and two pairs, or potentially a concealed pung if B7 is drawn.\n\nAnswer: Play J2"}
